Neuromancer (Sprawl; book 1), New York, N.Y.: Ace Books, →ISBN, page 9:"}, {"text": "He spent nights cruising queer bars near the pad, saw Wiltsie at the dives, but always in the company of his squeeze, a guy he called 'Duane.'", "reference": "1988, James Ellroy, Dudley Smith Trio: The Big Nowhere, LA Confidential, White Jazz, Random House, →ISBN, page 459:"}, {"text": "His young squeeze had just backed out and had not seen the assault on her “sugar daddy” when it happened!", "reference": "2012, J. Lamar, Tip Tap Toe, Xlibris Corporation, →ISBN, page 141:"}, {"text": "But even considering that, he might have been a bit more restrained if he hadn't run into his former sexy squeeze, Penny Atieno.", "reference": "2014, N. Lombardi Jr., Journey Towards a Falling Sun, John Hunt Publishing, →ISBN:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "ficante"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(slang) An illicit alcoholic drink made by squeezing Sterno through cheesecloth, etc., and mixing the result with fruit juice.", "tags": ["countable", "slang", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(baseball) The act of bunting in an attempt to score a runner from third.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": ["The game ended in exciting fashion with a failed squeeze."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "ja", "name": "Japanese"}, "word": "スクイズ"}, {"language": {"code": "ko", "name": "Korean"}, "word": "스퀴즈"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(card games) A play that forces an opponent to discard a card that gives up one or more tricks.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(caving) A traversal of a narrow passage.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": ["It was a tight squeeze, but I got through to the next section of the cave."], "quotes": [{"text": "The most notorious squeezes have names: the Gun Barrel, Jam Crack, the Electric Armpit Crawl, Devil's Pinch.", "reference": "2003, Barbara Hurd, “The Squeeze”, in Entering the Stone: On Caves and Feeling through the Dark, Boston, Mass.: Houghton Mifflin Company, →ISBN, page 11:"}, {"text": "Prior to going back out to Mystery Cave again we spent a lot of time preparing. We made a squeeze box, which is a wooden box the opening of which can be adjusted in size. We could then crawl through the opening and measure to see how tight of a squeeze we could fit through.", "reference": "2016, Diego Rodriguez, The Caver: Dig ... But Not to Far, Munich: BookRix, →ISBN:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "A moulding, cast or other impression of an object, chiefly a design, inscription etc., especially by pressing wet paper onto the surface and peeling off when dry.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Nollekens, finding his wife always benefited by these visits, never refused White a squeeze of a patera, or any thing that would answer his purpose; […] White […] had turned his wine-cellars into manufactories for the produce of cast coins, and moderns squeezes from Roman lamps.", "reference": "1828, JT Smith, Nollekens and His Times, Century Hutchinson, published 1986, page 65:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(mining) The gradual closing of workings by the weight of the overlying strata.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(dated) The situation experienced by a middleman when pressured from both sides, especially financially.", "tags": ["countable", "dated", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Thus was established a powerful Chinese combination, which maintained itself by submitting to a heavy \"squeeze\" at the hands of the Viceroy and Governor of Canton on the one hand and of the Hoppo on the other.", "reference": "1898, Archibald R. Colquhoun, China in Transformation, page 47:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(dated, countable, uncountable) A bribe, fee, or extortionary price paid to a middleman, especially in China; the practice of requiring such a bribe or fee.", "tags": ["countable", "dated", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "If the licence […] was costly, it secured to them uninterrupted and extraordinary pecuniary advantages; but on the other hand it subjected them to 'calls' or 'squeezes' for contributions to public works, […] for the relief of districts suffering from scarcity […] as well as for the often imaginary […] damage caused by the overflowing of the 'Yangtse Keang' or the 'Yellow River.'", "reference": "1882, William C. Hunter, The \"Fan Kwae\" at Canton before treaty days 1825-1844:"}, {"text": "The mattress shop had been bought with the proceeds of squeeze obtained by him from a former American employer.", "reference": "1928, China Digest, volume 10, page 10:"}, {"text": "They were no colonists; their administration was merely a squeeze, and nothing more, I suspect.", "reference": "1899 February, Joseph Conrad, “The Heart of Darkness”, in Blackwood’s Edinburgh Magazine, volume CLXV, number M, New York, N.Y.: The Leonard Scott Publishing Company, […], →OCLC, part I, page 196:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(UK, slang, obsolete) A person's neck.", "tags": ["UK", "countable", "obsolete", "slang", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "\"Got his description putty close: Short black 'air, black whiskers, with a crips^([sic]) curl at the hedges; a white choker, tight round his squeeze; dressed in black, and orful hugly,\" remarked the policeman.", "reference": "1860, The London Journal, page 146:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squeeze", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}